WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.044 --> 00:00:18.945
storm ended just as quickly as it began— almost as if it had never happened.

2
00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:23.367
The next day was sunny, beautiful, and calm once again.

3
00:00:24.407 --> 00:00:27.268
The boat, however, did not survive the wind and rain.

4
00:00:28.256 --> 00:00:32.999
When Tommy opened his eyes, he found himself still holding onto the mast.

5
00:00:35.821 --> 00:00:37.823
There were pieces of wood everywhere.

6
00:00:38.503 --> 00:00:41.165
Tommy even saw the boat's wheel floating by.

7
00:00:41.806 --> 00:00:43.627
But there were no signs of Dr.

8
00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:45.988
Dolittle, Charles, or Polynesia.

9
00:00:46.649 --> 00:00:47.710
He was all alone.

10
00:00:50.492 --> 00:00:54.354
"I will not cry," Tommy said as he wiped away his tears.

11
00:00:54.374 --> 00:00:56.536
"They are alive, I know it!"

12
00:00:57.156 --> 00:00:59.298
Tommy tried to think of happy thoughts.

13
00:01:00.198 --> 00:01:01.319
"Someone will find me.

14
00:01:01.819 --> 00:01:05.141
I will be together with my friends again," he said aloud.

15
00:01:05.942 --> 00:01:09.524
At that moment, Tommy looked into the water and screamed.

16
00:01:10.985 --> 00:01:13.727
There were two scary sharks swimming around him.

17
00:01:13.747 --> 00:01:16.689
"Go away, please," he whispered.

18
00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:19.731
One shark poked his head out of the water.

19
00:01:19.751 --> 00:01:23.294
"He doesn't look too good," he said to his friend.

20
00:01:24.134 --> 00:01:26.676
The other came out of the water and looked at Tommy.

21
00:01:27.536 --> 00:01:29.557
"Not much meat on him, is there?"

22
00:01:29.577 --> 00:01:34.139
"Did you find anything else around?

23
00:01:34.439 --> 00:01:35.519
Something tastier?"

24
00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:37.640
the first shark licked its lips.

25
00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:44.283
"Nope. This small human is the only thing I can see," the second one said.

26
00:01:45.063 --> 00:01:47.284
Tommy wished he could speak their language.

27
00:01:47.985 --> 00:01:50.546
He decided to use what he had already learned.

28
00:01:50.566 --> 00:01:56.008
"Oink, quack, hee-haw, woof-woof," he said.

29
00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:00.328
The sharks looked confused.

30
00:02:00.969 --> 00:02:01.929
"What's he doing?"

31
00:02:02.369 --> 00:02:02.829
one asked.

32
00:02:02.849 --> 00:02:05.530
"Don't ask me," said the other.

33
00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:08.651
"I can never understand these humans."

34
00:02:08.671 --> 00:02:10.871
"Shall we eat him or not?"

35
00:02:11.611 --> 00:02:16.173
But before they could decide, a long, horrible screeching sound was heard.

36
00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:20.774
Tommy and the sharks looked up.

37
00:02:20.794 --> 00:02:24.035
"Polynesia!" cried Tommy joyfully.

38
00:02:24.935 --> 00:02:28.056
She swooped down and started to bite the sharks' noses.

39
00:02:28.876 --> 00:02:29.716
"Shame on you!

40
00:02:30.036 --> 00:02:31.817
Trying to eat a helpless boy!"

41
00:02:32.277 --> 00:02:33.157
she scolded them.

42
00:02:33.177 --> 00:02:34.958
"That hurts!"

43
00:02:35.378 --> 00:02:39.399
"Aw!" the sharks cried and dived back into the water.

44
00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:44.700
Tommy was so happy to see his friend.

45
00:02:45.341 --> 00:02:46.821
He could not stop crying.

46
00:02:46.841 --> 00:02:51.322
"Now, now, Tommy," said the parrot, comforting him.

47
00:02:51.342 --> 00:02:53.063
"What about the doctor?

48
00:02:53.563 --> 00:02:55.423
Charles?" Tommy sobbed.

49
00:02:55.443 --> 00:02:57.744
"We're all safe."

50
00:02:58.688 --> 00:03:01.270
Polynesia explained everything that had happened.

51
00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:04.932
"The doctor and Charles are on land, waiting for you.

52
00:03:05.792 --> 00:03:08.194
So we should go to them as soon as possible."

53
00:03:08.214 --> 00:03:09.354
"But how?"

54
00:03:09.794 --> 00:03:10.395
asked Tommy.

55
00:03:10.415 --> 00:03:12.576
"I don't have anything to row with."

56
00:03:13.577 --> 00:03:15.918
"We don't need oars," she replied.

57
00:03:15.938 --> 00:03:17.779
"Our friends will help us."

58
00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.342
Tommy suddenly felt the mast gliding along in the water.

59
00:03:22.362 --> 00:03:26.004
"Hold on tight," Polynesia called out.

60
00:03:26.732 --> 00:03:29.953
Tommy turned around to see two beautiful dolphins.

61
00:03:30.733 --> 00:03:34.154
They were using their long noses to push the mast forward.

62
00:03:34.794 --> 00:03:38.655
Tommy wanted to reach out and touch their smooth, shiny skin.

63
00:03:38.675 --> 00:03:42.676
"Everything okay?"

64
00:03:43.137 --> 00:03:45.177
Polynesia called out to the dolphins.

65
00:03:45.197 --> 00:03:46.958
"It certainly is!

66
00:03:47.318 --> 00:03:48.738
He's light as a feather!"

67
00:03:49.178 --> 00:03:49.798
one replied.

68
00:03:49.818 --> 00:03:51.539
"Not like Dr.

69
00:03:51.599 --> 00:03:54.940
Dolittle and that other man," called out the other.

70
00:03:55.716 --> 00:03:58.738
"Now that was heavy!"

71
00:03:59.158 --> 00:04:01.000
The dolphins laughed out cheerfully.

72
00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:04.562
"Yes, Dr.

73
00:04:04.602 --> 00:04:07.644
Dolittle told me he'd put on some weight," laughed Tommy.

74
00:04:08.304 --> 00:04:10.066
Polynesia stared at Tommy.

75
00:04:10.726 --> 00:04:14.168
The dolphins stopped pushing and poked their heads out of the water.

76
00:04:14.869 --> 00:04:17.571
Tommy did not know why everyone was looking at him.

77
00:04:17.591 --> 00:04:19.492
"Did I say something wrong?"

78
00:04:19.912 --> 00:04:20.813
he asked shyly.

79
00:04:20.833 --> 00:04:29.195
"Tommy," Polynesia said finally, "just now, you understood our language and spoke it."

80
00:04:29.215 --> 00:04:32.578
"What?" Tommy shook his head in confusion.

81
00:04:33.458 --> 00:04:35.300
He thought about what had just happened.

82
00:04:36.241 --> 00:04:39.563
Yes, he clearly understood what the dolphins said.

83
00:04:39.583 --> 00:04:41.325
"Oh, my!"

84
00:04:41.665 --> 00:04:42.386
he exclaimed.

85
00:04:42.406 --> 00:04:43.927
"I can speak!

86
00:04:44.327 --> 00:04:45.108
I can speak!"

87
00:04:48.191 --> 00:04:50.272
Soon, Tommy saw the island ahead.

88
00:04:51.053 --> 00:04:54.356
Dr. Dolittle and Charles were waving their hands excitedly.

89
00:04:55.124 --> 00:05:01.295
Tommy did not know what made him happier: seeing his friends again or finally being able to speak

90
00:05:01.435 --> 00:05:02.276
animal language.

91
00:05:03.198 --> 00:05:06.263
He decided that both things made him equally happy.
